MOUNT(1)                    User Commands                    MOUNT(1)

NAME
    mount - mount and unmount filesystems

SYNOPSIS
    mount
    mount [-o options] type source target
    mount -u target

DESCRIPTION
    Without arguments mount lists the mounted filesystems from /dev/mounts.
    With a type, a source device under /dev and a target directory it
    mounts the filesystem. -o passes a comma separated option string to
    the filesystem, such as uid=1000,gid=1000,umask=077 for fat, which
    sets the owner and the permissions of every file of the volume
    (fstab(5)). -u unmounts the filesystem at target.

EXAMPLES
    mount mfs vdb /mnt
    mount -o uid=1000,gid=1000 fat vdd /mnt/usb
    mount -u /mnt

SEE ALSO
    fstab(5), fsinit(1), df(1)
